# 8. Experimental Protocol

## 8.1 Data Splitting

Each benchmark is divided into three conceptual subsets:

```text
                 Full optimization data
                         |
              +----------+----------+
              |                     |
           Mining                 Validation
              |                     |
              +----------+----------+
                         |
                    optimization
                         |
                    [SEALED]
                         |
                         v
                       Test
```

The mining set provides examples that can be shown directly to the optimizer.

The validation set is used to evaluate candidate prompt behavior during optimization but is not used as the final test set.

The test set remains sealed until optimization has completed.

---

## 8.2 Multi-Seed Evaluation

Because LLM outputs can vary even under nominally deterministic decoding, every principal configuration is evaluated across multiple independent seeds.

We use:

$$
N_{\text{seeds}} = [3/5]
$$

independent runs per solver × benchmark × optimization method configuration.

We report:

* mean;
* standard deviation;
* median;
* 95% confidence interval;
* per-seed results; and
* paired item-level differences where appropriate.

The single-seed experiments conducted during development revealed substantial variability. Four identical LegalBench-Hearsay Reflective-FDPO configurations produced final test accuracies of 0.735, 0.755, 0.816, and 0.857, demonstrating that single-run differences of only a few percentage points can be difficult to interpret at these evaluation-set sizes.

This motivates our use of multi-seed evaluation in the final experimental protocol.

