## 14.3 Accept-Margin Gate

An earlier version of Reflective-FDPO reverted the entire optimization trajectory when the final validation score fell below the baseline by a fixed margin.

We removed this gate because repeated runs showed that validation scores at \(n\approx25-32\) can fluctuate substantially.

This provides an important methodological lesson:

> **A noisy validation estimate should not necessarily be treated as reliable evidence that an optimization trajectory is harmful.**

The final method therefore retains the best committed round rather than applying a hard accept/reject decision based on a single noisy validation comparison.

