```

but may be smaller than the run-to-run variation of the underlying evaluation process.

We therefore report multi-seed distributions rather than relying on individual trajectories.

This is especially important for benchmarks with only 30–66 test examples. Approximate binomial standard errors are large at such sample sizes, and model sampling can introduce additional variation.

