# Appendix E. Main Claim to Preserve

The paper should ultimately make **one central claim**:

> **Reflective-FDPO improves feedback-driven prompt optimization by exposing the optimizer to the item-level consequences of its previous edits, allowing it to reason about both recoveries and regressions on mining and validation examples.**

It should **not** claim:

> "Reflective-FDPO universally outperforms GEPA/MIPROv2/ProTeGi."

Unless a later experiment establishes that under genuinely matched conditions.

The strongest version of the paper is instead:

> **Outcome-aware reflection is a distinct and measurable source of optimization signal, and its benefit can be isolated through controlled Simple-FDPO versus Reflective-FDPO experiments.**
